1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,149
What if an AI assistant could not move on until reality proved the last step actually happened?

2
00:00:07,149 --> 00:00:10,513
Meet GroundStep, a Codex-native guide for physical tasks.

3
00:00:11,713 --> 00:00:15,737
This real test begins with a disconnected DIGI router.

4
00:00:15,737 --> 00:00:19,762
GroundStep exposes only one bounded instruction: inspect the hardware.

5
00:00:19,762 --> 00:00:27,812
The photo shows the router, loose cable ends, and a dry work surface, so the step is verified.

6
00:00:27,812 --> 00:00:32,284
A close-up then identifies WAN without relying on cable color.

7
00:00:33,484 --> 00:00:37,418
The user connects the black cable to LAN one.

8
00:00:37,418 --> 00:00:40,042
Codex can clearly read the labels.

9
00:00:40,042 --> 00:00:41,353
WAN is empty.

10
00:00:41,353 --> 00:00:46,600
GroundStep records a ninety-nine percent mismatch and keeps the service check locked.

11
00:00:46,600 --> 00:00:49,660
The workflow cannot be talked into advancing.

12
00:00:50,860 --> 00:00:58,004
A second angle shows cables in multiple ports, but cannot prove which one is the incoming line.

13
00:00:58,004 --> 00:01:00,526
GroundStep chooses uncertain instead of guessing.

14
00:01:00,526 --> 00:01:09,771
A wider photo resolves the ambiguity: the incoming black cable is visibly seated in WAN, so exactly one next step is unlocked.

15
00:01:10,971 --> 00:01:15,599
The first status photo is red, so completion is rejected.

16
00:01:15,599 --> 00:01:19,765
The next photo shows the known connected green state.

17
00:01:19,765 --> 00:01:23,004
Only now does GroundStep complete the case.

18
00:01:23,004 --> 00:01:27,633
Seven photographs produced four verified steps and three blocked attempts.

19
00:01:28,833 --> 00:01:40,392
Every image is copied locally, hashed with S H A two fifty-six, and recorded with the verdict, explanation, confidence, and timestamp.

20
00:01:40,392 --> 00:01:42,043
Codex provides vision.

21
00:01:42,043 --> 00:01:44,245
Deterministic code controls progress.

22
00:01:44,245 --> 00:01:48,649
GroundStep: the model can suggest, but reality decides.

